":"agent_judgment","shared_sources":"n/a"},"needs_research":[],"would_satisfy_once_confirmed":["original_text","clause_inventory","ending_or_current_basis","counterevidence"]},"shared_sources":[],"signing_dates_seen":{"fr-originals@jobs/fr-originals/output":"1977-02-11","later-events_catalog":"1977-02-11","stage19_causal_queue":"1977-02-11"},"source_ladder_exhausted_proposed":[],"status":"MACHINE DRAFT - UNVERIFIED; not a claim; see jobs/claim-drafts/AGENT_GUIDE.md"},"claim":{"instrument_id":"EO:11971","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Source: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1977-02-15/pdf/FR-1977-02-15.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: b47dbf578e6002db07f8fa635e5358e891f4f10f3ac336d927ebc909eb777e1a\nLocation: 42 FR 9155, PDF pages 13-14 (confidence high)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"42 FR 9155, PDF pages 13-14; operative words before the numbered sections","sha256":"b47dbf578e6002db07f8fa635e5358e891f4f10f3ac336d927ebc909eb777e1a","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1977-02-15/pdf/FR-1977-02-15.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11971#preamble-op","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Section  1. Establishment of the Committee.  There is hereby established the \nCommittee on Selection of the Director of the Federal Bureau of Investigation, herein­\nafter referred to as the Committee. The Committee shall consist of a Chairman and \neight other members to be appointed by the President.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"42 FR 9155, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 1","sha256":"b47dbf578e6002db07f8fa635e5358e891f4f10f3ac336d927ebc909eb777e1a","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1977-02-15/pdf/FR-1977-02-15.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11971#sec1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 2. Functions. The Committee.shall conduct inquiries to identify persons who \nmay be qualified to serve as the Director of the Federal Bureau of Investigation, \nhereinafter referred to as the Director, and shall conduct investigations of those \npersons to determine their qualifications.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"42 FR 9155, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 2","sha256":"b47dbf578e6002db07f8fa635e5358e891f4f10f3ac336d927ebc909eb777e1a","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1977-02-15/pdf/FR-1977-02-15.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11971#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The Committee shall submit to the President and to the Attorney General,\nwithin ninety days from the date of this Order, a report listing the names of the five \npersons whom the Committee considers best qualified to serve as the Director and \nsetting forth such other information as the President or the Attorney General may \nrequire. . .  „\n(b) The Committee shall terminate thirty days after submission of its report, \nunless its duration is extended by the President. So, long as the Committee remains \nin existence, it shall conduct such additional inquiries and submit such additional \nreports as may be requested by the President or the Attorney General.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"42 FR 9155, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 3(a)","sha256":"b47dbf578e6002db07f8fa635e5358e891f4f10f3ac336d927ebc909eb777e1a","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1977-02-15/pdf/FR-1977-02-15.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11971#sec3(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 4. Ineligibility of Committee Members.  No member of the. Committee shall \nbe eligible to be considered as a possible nominee for the position of Director.\nSeCi. 5. Cooperation by Executive Agencies.  The Committee is authorized to \nrequest, through its Chairman, from any Executive department or agency such \ninformation or assistance as the Committee deems necessary to carry out its functions \nunder this Order. Each department or agency shall, to the extent permitted by law, \nfurnish such information or assistance to the Committee. The Committee also is \nauthorized to request from any State agency such information and assistance as the \nCommittee deems necessary, and to obtain such information and assistance to the \nextént permitted by State law.\nFEDERAL REGISTER, VOL. 42, N O . 31— TUESDAY, FEBRUARY 15, 19 77\n\n=== PDF page 14 of 216 ===\n9156 TH E  PRESIDENT\nSec. 6. Travel Expenses; Administrative Support; Financing.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"42 FR 9155, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 4 (lead-in)","sha256":"b47dbf578e6002db07f8fa635e5358e891f4f10f3ac336d927ebc909eb777e1a","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1977-02-15/pdf/FR-1977-02-15.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11971#sec4","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Members of the Committee shall serve without compensation. While \nengaged in the work of the Committee, members may receive travel expenses, includ­\ning per diem in lieu of subsistence, as authorized by law (5 U.S.C. 5702 and 5703).","original_source":{"page_or_item":"42 FR 9155, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 4(a)","sha256":"b47dbf578e6002db07f8fa635e5358e891f4f10f3ac336d927ebc909eb777e1a","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1977-02-15/pdf/FR-1977-02-15.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11971#sec4(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Attorney General shall furnish to the Committee necessary staff, sup­\nplies, facilities and other administrative services.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"42 FR 9155, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 4(b)","sha256":"b47dbf578e6002db07f8fa635e5358e891f4f10f3ac336d927ebc909eb777e1a","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1977-02-15/pdf/FR-1977-02-15.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11971#sec4(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) All necessary expenses incurred in connection with the work of the Com­\nmittee, to the extent permitted by law, shall be paid from funds available to the \nAttorney General.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"42 FR 9155, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 4(c)","sha256":"b47dbf578e6002db07f8fa635e5358e891f4f10f3ac336d927ebc909eb777e1a","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1977-02-15/pdf/FR-1977-02-15.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11971#sec4(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 7. Federal Advisory Committee Act Functions.  Notwithstanding the provi­\nsions of any other Executive order, the functions of the President under the Federal \nAdvisory Committee Act (5 U.S.C. App. I ), except that of reporting annually to the \nCongress, which are applicable to the Committee, shall be performed by the Attorney \nGeneral in accordance with guidelines and procedures established by the Office of \nManagement and Budget.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"42 FR 9155, PDF pages 13-14; Sec. 7","sha256":"b47dbf578e6002db07f8fa635e5358e891f4f10f3ac336d927ebc909eb777e1a","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1977-02-15/pdf/FR-1977-02-15.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11971#sec7","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"42 FR 9155, PDF pages 13-14","sha256":"b47dbf578e6002db07f8fa635e5358e891f4f10f3ac336d927ebc909eb777e1a","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1977-02-15/pdf/FR-1977-02-15.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 9 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:11971"}
